cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "BioPyTools: A modular command-line toolkit for reproducible bioinformatics workflows"
version: "1.74.1"
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Xiang
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8400-7116"
    email: lixiang117423@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Yazhouwan National Laboratory, Sanya, Hainan, China"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lixiang117423/biopytools"
url: "https://lixiang117423.github.io/biopytools/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  BioPyTools is a Python command-line toolkit for reproducible bioinformatics
  workflows, with modules for sequencing-data quality control, genome assembly
  and annotation, variant analysis, pangenomics, phylogenetics, population
  genetics, microbiome analysis, and effector prediction.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - computational biology
  - command-line interface
  - reproducible research
  - high-performance computing
  - plant genomics
